    if (!household.isEmpty() && !sharesHousehold) {
        throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
    }
    owner.setTelephone(telephone);
    owner.setEmail(EmailNormalizer.normalize(owner.getEmail()));
    if (sharesHousehold) {
        this.clinicService.joinHousehold(owner, household);
    }
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    this.ownerAuditor.ownerCreated(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = toOwnerDtoWithBulkSignupWarning(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

**(b) Service persistence** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`, `saveOwner`, lines 242-253:
```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null) {
            owner.setCustomerCode(customerCodeGenerator.generate(owner));
        }
        owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCounter.count(owner));
    }
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

So on a new owner, `saveOwner` sets `customerCode` and `namesakeCount` — the latter is what feeds `getMembershipTier()`.

**Household join** — `ClinicServiceImpl.joinHousehold`, lines 290-302, assigns a stable `householdId` (via `HouseholdIdGenerator.generate`) to the new owner and back-fills existing members:
```java
@Override
@Transactional
public String joinHousehold(Owner owner, Collection<Owner> existingMembers) throws DataAccessException {
    String householdId = HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
    for (Owner member : existingMembers) {
        if (!householdId.equals(member.getHouseholdId())) {
            member.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(member);
        }
    }
    return householdId;
}
```

Supporting collaborators used in the flow:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/NamesakeCounter.java` — `count(Owner)` (lines 46-53) counts existing owners with matching normalized first+last name via `findByLastNameIgnoreCase`. This directly determines whether `namesakeCount == 0` (SILVER-eligible).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/CustomerCodeGenerator.java` — `generate(Owner)` (lines 49-52) builds `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/HouseholdIdGenerator.java` — `generate(lastName, address)` (lines 43-57), 16-char uppercase SHA-256 hex of normalized `lastName\naddress`.
- `findOwnersInHousehold` in `ClinicServiceImpl` (lines 279-288) filters `findByLastNameIgnoreCase` by normalized last name + address.
- `ownerAuditor.ownerCreated(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/OwnerAuditor.java`.

## 4. Owner repository interfaces + query methods

**Base interface:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`. Methods:
- `findByLastName(String)` (line 47) — prefix/starts-with match
- `findByLastName(String, Pageable)` (line 49)
- `findByTelephone(String)` (line 58)
- `findByLastNameIgnoreCase(String)` (line 68)
- `findById(int)` (line 77)
- `save(Owner)` (line 86)
- `findAll()` (line 94), `findAll(Pageable)` (line 96)
- `count()` (line 103)
- `countByCity(String)` (line 111)
- `countByRegistrationDate(LocalDate)` (line 119)
- `delete(Owner)` (line 127)

**Spring Data JPA impl:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` (`@Profile("spring-data-jpa")`, extends `OwnerRepository, Repository<Owner,Integer>`). Custom `@Query` overrides at lines 39-65:
- `findByLastName` (line 40): `... WHERE owner.lastName LIKE :lastName%` (with left join fetch pets)
- `findByLastName(..., Pageable)` (lines 44-47): `LIKE CONCAT(:lastName, '%')` + count query
- `findAll(Pageable)` (lines 50-53)
- `findById` (line 56): join fetch pets by id
- `findByTelephone` (line 60): exact telephone match
- `findByLastNameIgnoreCase` (line 64): `WHERE LOWER(owner.lastName) = LOWER(:lastName)`

**Other implementations of the same base interface** (profile-selected):
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`

(I did not open these two; they implement the same 12 methods for the `jpa` / `jdbc` profiles. Let me know if you want their internals.)

## 5. Tests related to membershipTier / owner creation

Only the acceptance test suite touches these concepts (no unit tests reference `membershipTier`, `namesakeCount`, `householdId`, `customerCode`, or `saveOwner`).

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — single test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold()` (lines 12-29). Builds a shared household (same `lastName` + `address`, `sharesHousehold=true`), creates 3 members, and asserts on the third: `jsonPath("$.membershipTier").value("GOLD")` (line 28). As noted in section 1, production code never returns `GOLD`, so this expectation is not satisfiable by the current `Owner.getMembershipTier()`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box base (all tests go through `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`). Relevant helpers: `ownerNode()` (lines 116-125, fully-unique valid owner, keeps namesakeCount at 0), `createOwnerOk` (line 160), `getOwner` (line 189), `uniqueLastName`/`uniqueAddress` used to force a shared household. Note `ownerNode()` does not set an `email`, which matters for SILVER vs BRONZE.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — audit-log test support (matched the grep on owner-creation terms via the auditor path).

No test directly exercises `NamesakeCounter`, `CustomerCodeGenerator`, `HouseholdIdGenerator`, or `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`/`joinHousehold` in isolation.

